<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Greatest velocity of a particle</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A particle \(P\) moves along a straight line so that its displacement from \(O\) after \(t\) seconds is \(s = {@s@}\) metres, \(t \ge 0\).</p><p>(a) Find the time at which the velocity of \(P\) is greatest.</p><div>\(t =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the greatest velocity.</p><div>[[input:ans2]] \(\text{m/s}\) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) \(P\) is at rest when \(t = 0\). When is it next at rest?</p><div>\(t =\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div><p>(d) Find the acceleration of \(P\) at that moment.</p><div>[[input:ans4]] \(\text{m/s}^2\) [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(v = \dfrac{ds}{dt} = {@v@}\) and \(a = \dfrac{dv}{dt} = {@a@}\).</p><p>(a) The velocity is greatest when its rate of change, the acceleration, is zero: \(a = 0\) at \(t = {@m0@}\). Before that \(a \gt 0\) and \(v\) is increasing; after it \(a \lt 0\) and \(v\) is decreasing, so this is the greatest velocity.</p><p>(b) \(v = {@vmax@}\,\text{m/s}\) at \(t = {@m0@}\).</p><p>(c) \(v = {@3*c0*t*(2*m0-t)@} = 0\) at \(t = 0\) and \(t = {@tr@}\).</p><p>(d) At \(t = {@tr@}\), \(a = {@a2@}\,\text{m/s}^2\). The velocity is \(0\) but the acceleration is negative, so \(P\) is about to move back towards \(O\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>4</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: s = c0(3 m0 t^2 - t^3): greatest velocity at t = m0 (a = 0), next at rest at t = 2 m0. Source: original. */
L: [[1,2],[2,3],[1,4],[2,2],[1,5],[3,2],[1,3],[2,4],[1,6],[3,3]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
c0: L[ix][1]; m0: L[ix][2];
s: expand(c0*(3*m0*t^2-t^3));
v: diff(s,t); a: diff(v,t);
vmax: 3*c0*m0^2; tr: 2*m0; a2: -6*c0*m0;
sm: ev(s,t=m0); a0v: ev(a,t=0);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
